nPolicy Office\nThe Office of University Policy (Policy Office or OUP) administers the University\u2019s\nprocess for developing and managing its comprehensive repository of University Policies,\nwhich encompasses University regulations, Board of Trustees Policies, University Policies, manuals, guides, and internal operating procedures. The\nPolicy Office plays an indispensable role in guiding and assisting University policy\nowners in the development and revision of policies, ensuring a consistent and transparent\nprocedure. Additionally, OUP manages the publication, archiving of policies, and offers\nguidance on policy-related inquiries and education. Notwithstanding the role of the\nOUP, responsibility for a policy\u2019s content resides with the policy-owner.\nOn this website you will find the official library of University Policies, related\ninformation and resources and contact information to assist with the policy development\nand approval process. Policies reproduced on other websites or in print might not\nrepresent the most current version. OUP encourages you to explore the Resources section\non this page to access valuable information.\nUNIVERSITY POLICIES\nRegulations, Policies and Procedures Library\nManuals, Handbooks & Collective Bargaining Agreements\nManuals\nCollective Bargaining Agreements\nPOLICY OFFICE RESOURCES\nCreating or Revising a Policy\nTemplates\nChecklists and Flowcharts\nPolicy Hierarchy\nPolicy FAQ\nPolicy Advisory Committee\nSTATE RESOURCES\nFlorida Board of Governors\nFlorida Statutes\nFlorida Sunshine Manuals\nContact Us\nOffice of University Policy\n1735 Althea Gibson Way\nSuite 101\nCASS Building\nTallahassee, Florida 32307\nP:\n(850) 599-8330\nE:\npolicies@famu.edu\nShira R. Thomas, Esq.\nChief Policy Officer and University Counsel\nshira.thomas@famu.edu\nAbigail V. Raddar\nPolicy Program Manager\nabigail.raddar@famu.edu\nSharon L. Snelling\nPolicy Coordinator\nsharon.snelling@famu.edu\nApply\nVisit\nGive\nfab button\nBack to To